<!-- The D. Del. Bankruptcy adversary complaint's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs;
     docs/EVAL-LOOP.md, "Cross-engine gate") in the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; no face is
     named for pleadings, see ../README.md) at 12 pt (size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (480
     twips, typst pitch-body: double spaced) with a half-inch first-line indent (typst para-indent); single lines in
     14 pt boxes (280 twips, typst pitch-single). docx/deb-adversary-complaint.lua writes every paragraph itself: the
     court line, the two Form 416 captions (LR 9004-1(a)), the title, the numbered allegations (FRCP 10(b)), the
     headings, the prayer, the notes, the signature block, the footer (the page number, centred, its line box ending
     0.5 in above the edge: typst footer-descent) and the section (letter, 1 in margins). Twips: 20 x pt.
     pandoc-from: CommonMark with smart punctuation, as typst's cmarker reads the body ("a)" stays text). -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" pandoc-from="commonmark+smart+yaml_metadata_block" size="24" body="480" single="280" indent="720" heading="480" heading-before="0" heading-after="0" footer="720">
</reference>
